                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Dry British humor in a classic point and click adventure style. The story is interesting, some of it is funny with a parody style of general sci-fi elements.\n\nBut the main reason I can't outright recommend this is that it was very clearly designed as the first part of a series, and ten years later that series is fully abandoned. The story is relatively short and ends with a cliffhanger that will never be resolved.\n\nIf you can pick it up cheap and don't mind it being the scraps of a series that will never finish, that's on you. It's mildly entertaining but with no pay off due to the cliffhanger. A game in this style is all about the story and this one has too many loose ends.\n---\n\nBottom line: A mildly interesting start to a story that will never be completed.\n---\n\n[url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/38232109/]While you are here, would you consider following my curator page?[/url]\n\n[url=https://steamcommunity.com/id/kunovega/recommended/]Want to read all of my reviews and not just the curated ones?[/url]",
